With the provisioning services enabled, the next step is to define and
customize a system image that can subsequently be used to provision one or more
*compute* nodes. The following subsections highlight this process.

#### Build initial BOS image {% raw %}{#sec-assemble_bos}{% endraw %}

{{ warewulf }} 4 supports using container images as the base file system for
provisioning, and it can import these directly from an OCI registry like
Docker Hub. Container images must be created especially for use with {{ warewulf }}
since they need to include things like a kernel and an init system. In this
example we will import our base image from a set maintained by the {{ warewulf }}
community on the GitHub container registry.

The `wwctl image exec` command runs the commands below it, these commands
also be run interactively one a time with the command `wwctl image
shell {{ baseos }}`. You can add `/bin/false` as the last command to prevent
the image from rebuilding (it will show an error) and rebuild later with the
`wwctl image build` command.

<!-- begin_ohpc_run -->
<!-- ohpc_comment_header Create compute image for Warewulf -->
```bash
# Import the base image from Warewulf
[sms]# wwctl image import docker://ghcr.io/warewulf/warewulf-{{ osimage }} \
	{{ baseos }} --syncuser

# Define chroot location
[sms]# CHROOT=$(wwctl image show {{ baseos }})
[sms]# export CHROOT

# Enable OpenHPC inside image and update image.
#Disable image build on exit, rebuild later.
[sms]# wwctl image exec --build=false {{ baseos }} -- /bin/bash -ex <<- EOF
  dnf -y install dnf-utils
  dnf -y install http://repos.openhpc.community/OpenHPC/4/{{ ostree }}/\
{{ arch }}/ohpc-release-4-1.{{ ostag }}.{{ arch }}.rpm
  dnf -y update
EOF
```
<!-- end_ohpc_run -->
